# Drydock Berth 4

## Current Model

**Drydock berth 4** is the heavy-lift zone reserved Seaglass-only during SG-REFIT. The corrected **crane booking 2026-05-19** is ground truth once drydock opened — Victor Hale confirmed the **seaglass crane** on berth that morning and the **may 19 crane** date matches the vendor hold letter. Hull penetration stayed blocked until Victor Hale's spare thrust bearing staged port-side. An earlier preliminary email cited May 12 after Marcus Holt conflated the booking with a pier crane availability survey.

## Evidence

- `2026-04-29-seaglass-crane-prelim` - Marcus Holt forwarded Victor Hale's preliminary quote citing **seaglass crane** lift slot **crane booking 2026-05-12** at berth 4 heavy-lift zone; hull penetration blocked until spare thrust bearing lands port-side.
- `2026-05-19-drydock-morning-sync` - Victor Hale confirmed **seaglass crane** on berth with **crane booking 2026-05-19**, not May 12; **may 19 crane** is on the vendor hold letter now that drydock is live; Marcus directed retraction of the May 12 note in the sailing impact doc.

## Use In Work

- Schedule berth 4 crane windows and sailing impact docs against **2026-05-19** — treat the drydock morning sync as authoritative over the week-2 preliminary email.
- Block hull-penetration sign-off until thrust bearing is staged port-side per Victor Hale's drydock gate, independent of crane date corrections.

## Limits

Drydock berth 4 governs SG-REFIT heavy-lift at Pier 4 — not Pier 9 contractor staging or gangway delivery holds. An earlier note in `2026-04-29-seaglass-crane-prelim` incorrectly listed crane booking 2026-05-12; ground truth is 2026-05-19.

## Connections

