# Pier 9 Single-Contractor Plan

## Current Model

The **Pier 9 Single-Contractor Plan** was Victor Dunn's unified Pier 9 contracting envelope naming **Kelwick Marine** for all gate and gangway work under one mobilization, shared badge pool, and single liability rider. The **single-contractor plan** covered both **gate retrofit** and **gangway replacement** at Q2 kickoff while P9-GATE and P9-GANG codenames went live in the **terminal readiness playbook** tracker. Victor Dunn formally retired the **pier 9 single-contractor** track on **2026-05-06** citing **scope divergence** — gate automation and gangway hydraulic specs could not share one Kelwick envelope.

**Status:** Inactive — **superseded single-contractor** execution moved to split vendor tracks under the Q2 Terminal Readiness Playbook: P9-GATE / Turnstile Dynamics and P9-GANG / Bridgeway Hoist. Kelwick Marine remains on the old plan for audit trail only.

## Evidence

- `2026-04-20-q2-kickoff-terminal` - Week-1 kickoff shows P9-GATE and P9-GANG still rolling up under Victor Dunn's **Pier 9 Single-Contractor Plan** with **Kelwick Marine** as vendor of record — single mobilization, shared badge pool, one liability rider covering both scopes until procurement splits.
- `2026-05-06-single-contractor-superseded` - Victor Dunn formally retired the **pier 9 single-contractor** envelope effective **2026-05-06** with slide title **scope divergence**; **Kelwick Marine** remains named on the old **single-contractor plan** for audit trail while P9-GATE moves to Turnstile Dynamics and P9-GANG to Bridgeway Hoist.

## Use In Work

- Do not quote Kelwick Marine or this plan as active Pier 9 vendor guidance after 2026-05-06 — treat as superseded audit reference only.
- When retrieving Pier 9 vendor history, distinguish the Kelwick single contractor era (weeks 1–2) from the split-vendor track under the Q2 Terminal Readiness Playbook.

## Limits

This inactive plan does not govern post-split PO tracks, badge batches, delivery schedules, or change-order caps. Derek Blunt's 2026-04-27 vendor-split email already directed quotes to Turnstile Dynamics and Bridgeway Hoist before formal supersession.

## Connections

- [[decision-supersede-single-contractor]] - Decision retiring the unified Kelwick envelope after scope divergence.
- [[kelwick-marine]] - Vendor named on this plan for audit trail only.
- [[victor-dunn]] - Infrastructure program manager who authored and superseded this plan.
- [[plan-q2-terminal-readiness]] - Active plan that now tracks split P9-GATE and P9-GANG vendor execution.
