# Supersede Single-Contractor Decision

## Current Model

Victor Dunn formally retired the unified Pier 9 contracting envelope on **2026-05-06**. His slide title cited **scope divergence** — gate automation (Turnstile Dynamics) and gangway replacement (Bridgeway Hoist) diverged in schedule, liability, and hydraulic specs so one Kelwick Marine envelope could not cover both. The **superseded single-contractor** track moved to split vendor execution under the Q2 Terminal Readiness Playbook: P9-GATE / Turnstile Dynamics and P9-GANG / Bridgeway Hoist. Kelwick Marine remains named on the old pier 9 single-contractor plan for audit trail only.

## Evidence

- `2026-05-06-single-contractor-superseded` - Victor Dunn formally retired the **pier 9 single-contractor** envelope effective **2026-05-06** with slide title **scope divergence**; **superseded single-contractor** track splits to P9-GATE / Turnstile Dynamics and P9-GANG / Bridgeway Hoist under Q2 playbook while **Kelwick Marine** remains on old plan for audit trail only.

## Use In Work

- Treat any post-2026-05-06 Pier 9 vendor routing as split-track under the Q2 Terminal Readiness Playbook — do not resurrect Kelwick Marine as active vendor.
- When retrieving "single contractor" or "Kelwick" references, check date context: pre-05-06 historical vs post-05-06 superseded audit only.

## Limits

This decision retires unified contracting only — it does not itself assign vendor PO caps, badge batches, or delivery dates. Derek Blunt's 2026-04-27 vendor-split email preceded formal supersession by nine days.

## Connections

- [[plan-pier9-single-contractor]] - Inactive plan this decision retired.
